/target
**/*.rs.bk
node_modules/
media/*
!media/.gitkeep
*.log

# Generated at runtime: TLS material and saved device compensation. The key in
# particular must never be committed.
homesync-cert.pem
homesync-key.pem
homesync-cert-names.json
homesync-devices.json
*.json.tmp

# Fuzzing artefacts. The corpus is machine-generated and grows without bound;
# the targets and the harness are the parts worth keeping.
# `cargo fuzz` nests its working directories under fuzz/fuzz, so both depths
# are covered. The corpus in particular must stay out: it accumulates whatever
# was fed to it, which here included third-party sample audio.
/fuzz/target
/fuzz/Cargo.lock
**/corpus/
**/artifacts/

# Tracks fetched from a URL. The default download folder is the working
# directory, so without this the first fetch puts someone else's music in
# `git status` and one careless `git add .` commits it.
homesync-downloads/

# Demo recording intermediates. The finished animation is committed
# (docs/images/demo.gif); the PNG frames behind it and the WAVs the capture
# synthesises to fill the library are regenerated by docs/demo/capture.mjs and
# together run to tens of megabytes.
/docs/demo/frames/
/docs/demo/media/
